# Programs the old compiler accepts that the new compiler compiles without an error but that are on neither pass
# list (tests\corpus\slice.list, tests\upstream\pass.list), each with the reason (spec testing/compiler-tests,
# "Clean programs are listed"; study\archive\26 section 3). Shrink-only and kept by hand: tier 1 fails for a clean
# program on no list, and for an entry here that no longer compiles cleanly or that a pass list names.
corpus/runtime_comparison/126_print_comma.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/187_print_comma_zones.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/251_print_chain.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/80_print_semicolon.bas  # PRINT with a comma never ends when stdout is redirected (Windows console; KFAIL)
corpus/runtime_comparison/228_err_erl_values.bas  # its recording ends at a division by zero; here error 11 is trapped (QB64PE-DIVERGENCES.md D-052, libqb-fixes; KFAIL)
corpus/slice/s11_on_error.bas  # its recording ends at a division by zero; here error 11 is trapped (QB64PE-DIVERGENCES.md D-052, libqb-fixes; KFAIL)
corpus/slice/s17_operators.bas  # its recording ends at a division by zero; here error 11 is trapped (QB64PE-DIVERGENCES.md D-052, libqb-fixes; KFAIL)
upstream/const/math_funcs.bas  # checks _COTH(.2) against QB64pe's 2 * EXP(x) - 1; here the hyperbolic cotangent (QB64PE-DIVERGENCES.md D-031, const-rulings), so its COTH line prints -1  0
upstream/http/read_example.bas  # downloads www.example.com and compares it with a saved copy; the site changed (KFAIL, tools/legacy_tests/known_failures.txt)
upstream/noprompt/noprompt-continue-fatal.bas  # checks that a division by zero ends the program under QB64PE_NOPROMPT=continue; here error 11 is not critical (QB64PE-DIVERGENCES.md D-052, libqb-fixes), so the program goes on
